  "interpretation": [
    "A generic inability of libmpv/FFmpeg to read encoded URLs is disproven by these desktop controls. Neither relaxed extension checks nor forced HLS was shown necessary for successful playback.",
    "Nuvio current-main error text corresponds to an HTTP4xx access error, not a specific decoded-video failure. Exact rejected request and client difference on the phone remain unknown.",
    "Provider session.source supplies the wrapped transport. Standard opaque v2 object URLs are not a readable base64 upstream address. Beta contains an encoded signed upstream target that can be read for diagnosis.",
    "Fresh direct Beta masters were readable with upstream-origin headers, keeping all original parameters. Wrapper-origin headers produced403; blindly swapping URLs is not a validated fix.",
    "Both direct masters preserved video quality and audio-language inventory, but moved the default audio and exposed more native subtitle groups than the wrapper. A direct mode needs independent header/subtitle/default-audio handling and phone acceptance.",
    "No production URL decoding, source policy change, grant/session cache, extension-guard change, TLS bypass, player modification or plugin release was made."
  ],
